Taking \(g\) to be the function providing the meaning of and in (2), we can simplify the meaning derived above as follows:
\[I_{\textit{Eng.}}(\textit{Jo}) ∈ I_{\textit{Eng.}}(\textit{and})(I_{\textit{Eng.}}(\textit{jumps}), I_{\textit{Eng.}}(\textit{runs}))\] \[= \ct{j} ∈ g(\{\ct{j}\}, \{\ct{j}, \ct{b}\})\] \[= \ct{j} ∈ \{\ct{j}\} ∩ \{\ct{j}, \ct{b}\}\] \[= \ct{j} ∈ \{\ct{j}\}\] \[= \True\]


